**How to implement.** The reference half of `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` moves into the optics-mueller kit (001 §Q AT-1 'Data: … the reference pipeline's scripts, `README.md` and `reference_step1_summary.json` / `reference_step2_linear_summary.json` into `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`'; 001 §S9 'MOVE `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` into the AT-1 kit folder'; .spec-md §3.20 'The optics-mueller archive moves whole'; the S9.4 brief). `data.zip`, the measured data, moves in step 330, which deletes the folder. This step changes no code and no behaviour, and `MuellerReconstructionTests`' numbers are unchanged. (1) `git mv` each of these seven files from `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` to `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` under the same name: `README.md`, `cpl_cpl_analyzer.py`, `matrix_glue.py`, `matrix_step1_air_fit.py`, `matrix_fit_linear.py`, `reference_step1_summary.json` and `reference_step2_linear_summary.json`. The four scripts and the two summaries keep their bytes; they hold no carriage return, so the `*.py` and `*.json` rules of `.gitattributes` (`.gitattributes:25`, `:35`) change nothing in them. No `.kit-json` or other kit file is written: S12.1 builds the kit around these files. Under `data/`, `.gitignore` ignores only `/data/chroma/` and `/data/*/.oc/` (`.gitignore:333-334`), so `git check-ignore` matches none of the new paths. (2) In the moved `README.md` only what the move makes untrue changes, in the README's own voice: (a) its opening paragraph says that this folder, the optics-mueller kit's `data/reference/`, holds the reference implementation and the reference numerical results that `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs` was written against, and that the measured data it inventories is `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/data.zip`; (b) every other place that says `data.zip` is here (the paragraph after the provenance table, the `Measured data` table and the inventory sentence under it) names it by that repository path; (c) `Further reading` gains one bullet: `specs/0050/.manual/001-library-files-database-multi-setup-inverse.md` §Q AT-1 and §S9, which move this folder into the optics-mueller kit. Every other line keeps its text. (3) In `Berreman/BerremanTests/MuellerReconstructionTests.fs`, the comments that give the summaries' provenance name them at `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/`, and the README beside them as `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/README.md`: the class doc's spec 0044 §8.5 bullet ('`reference_step*_summary.json` in that same folder'), the acceptance-band comment above `stage1Tol` (`MuellerReconstructionTests.fs:stage1Tol`), the comment of `createArchiveBacked produces a MuellerDataProxy that loads every committed data set` that names the README's inventory, the provenance comment of `Stage-1 re-derived calibration constants match the reference pipeline's full-precision values`, and the two of `section 7.2 end-to-end: …` (in its spec 0044 §8.5 paragraph and above `expectedQz`). No code line changes. The other `Data/MuellerMatrix` texts under `Berreman/` change with what they describe: the class doc's bullet on `data.zip` and `loadDataSet`'s doc with the data (step 330), and the doc of `archiveEntryName` (`MuellerDataStore.fs:archiveEntryName`) with that member (step 331).

**Acceptance.** After the reference files move, `data/optics-mueller/data/reference/` MUST hold `README.md`, the four scripts and the two summaries, the scripts and summaries byte for byte, `Berreman/Data/MuellerMatrix/` MUST hold only `data.zip`, and `MuellerReconstructionTests` MUST name the summaries at their kit path; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class, `BerremanTests.MuellerReconstructionTests`, its numbers and count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s32 invariants MUST pass.
